 On web and desktop, a machine row and a project row below Search filter the sidebar.
 
-- **Machines**: Shown when two or more machines are known. A plain pick (or `Enter`) selects only that machine and closes the menu; picking the same single machine again clears it. `Cmd`-click (`Ctrl`-click outside macOS) adds or removes a machine and keeps the menu open. **All machines** clears the selection, as does selecting every machine. Projects stay available while they exist on any selected machine. Opening a thread on another machine returns the filter to **All machines**.
+- **Machines**: Shown when two or more machines are known. A plain pick (or `Enter`) selects only that machine and closes the menu; picking the same single machine again clears it. `Cmd`-click (`Ctrl`-click outside macOS) adds or removes a machine and keeps the menu open. **All machines** checks every machine; then `Cmd`/`Ctrl`-click the one you want to hide. Selecting every machine does the same as **All machines**. Projects stay available while they exist on any selected machine. Opening a thread on another machine returns the filter to **All machines**.
 - **Projects**: Click a project icon below the machine row (or below Search with one machine) to select only that project among the visible ones; click it again to clear the visible selection when it is the only selected project shown. Selections for projects on other machines stay saved. `Cmd`/`Ctrl`-click adds or removes a project. `Enter` and `Space` select only the focused project; `Cmd/Ctrl+Enter` adds or removes it. Picks keep the current Show only or Hide mode, including in **+N**. Right-click an icon to open its project settings. Archived projects are left out.
 - **+N and icon order**: **+N** opens the remaining projects with a search field. Pinned projects come first, then the others by name; to order them by latest thread activity or in your own order, change **Settings → Labs → Project icon order** (per device). With **Manual**, drag projects in the list below that setting, or move a focused handle with `Space` and the arrow keys; projects you have not placed yet follow by name. Pin a project in **+N**, or use the pin shortcut while its icon or search result is focused.
 - **Badges**: A project badge counts threads needing attention; a static dot means only working threads, and **+N** combines the projects that do not fit in the row. Hover an icon for its counts per state and a key to the badge colours.
